From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: VP9 video decoders (profile 0 and profile 2)

D3D11VA VP9 profile 0 (NV12) and profile 2 (10-bit, P010) decoders on
Vulkan Video (VK_KHR_video_decode_vp9, with its videoDecodeVP9 feature).
DXVA_PicParams_VP9 gives the frame header; the frame in the bitstream
buffer is handed over with where its uncompressed header, compressed
header and tiles start, and VP9 has no session parameters. The loop
filter deltas DXVA gives are those in force, handed over as updated.

Under Wine the extension is offered to 64-bit programs only (wine-sg
7848); where it is not offered, no VP9 decoder is. Offered only where
proven (d3d11.videoDecode): bit-exact against FFmpeg's software decoder
on NVIDIA's driver (libvpx profile 0 and 2, alt-ref frames, tiles,
segmentation).
